.TH FILEMGR 1 2026-09-27 "filemgr 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
filemgr \- keep your Downloads folder tidy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filemgr
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filemgr
sorts files into type folders, removes exact and near-duplicate copies,
archives stale files, applies user-defined cleanup rules, reports disk usage,
and can watch a folder to sort new downloads as they arrive.
.PP
By default it manages
.IR ~/Downloads .
It only ever moves files that sit directly in that folder or inside the
folders it manages itself (the category folders such as
.BR IMAGES ,
plus
.BR DUPLICATES ).
Folders you create yourself, such as
.BR PROTECTED ,
are never touched.
.PP
Nothing is ever deleted. Every move is recorded in a journal and can be
reversed with
.BR "filemgr undo" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sort
Move top-level files into type folders by extension.
.TP
.BR recent " [\fIn\fR]"
Bring the \fIn\fR most recently modified files back to the top level (default 5).
.TP
.BR dedup " [\fB\-\-near\fR] [\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fIN\fR]"
Move byte-identical duplicates into
.BR DUPLICATES/ ,
keeping the oldest copy. With
.BR \-\-near ,
also move visually similar images (resized, re-compressed or converted
copies) into
.BR DUPLICATES/NEAR/ ,
keeping the highest-resolution copy.
.I N
is the maximum perceptual-hash distance out of 64 (default 6).
.TP
.BR old " [\fIdays\fR]"
Move files not modified for \fIdays\fR or more (default 30) into
.BR OLD/ .
Files already in OLD/ are re-evaluated on each run.
.TP
.BR upload " \fIfolder\fR [\fB\-\-remote\fR \fINAME\fR]"
Copy a folder to Google Drive with
.BR rclone (1).
.TP
.BR watch " [\fB\-\-settle\fR \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\-existing\fR] [\fB\-\-print\-plist\fR]"
Stay running and sort each new file once it has finished downloading.
Partial downloads (.crdownload, .part, ...) are ignored.
.B \-\-print\-plist
prints a
.BR launchd (8)
agent for running at login.
.TP
.BR clean " [\fIrule\fR ...] [\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-\-names\fR]"
Apply the cleanup rules from the config file (see
.BR RULES ).
.TP
.BR stats " [\fB\-\-top\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-dups\fR] [\fB\-\-html\fR \fIFILE\fR]"
Report usage by type, folder and age, the largest files, and cleanup
opportunities. Read-only.
.TP
.BR find " [\fIpattern\fR ...] [\fIfilters\fR]"
Search by name (case-insensitive glob, or substring without wildcards).
Filters:
.BR \-\-type " \fICATEGORY\fR, " \-\-ext " \fILIST\fR, " \-\-larger " / " \-\-smaller " \fISIZE\fR, "
.BR \-\-older " / " \-\-newer " \fIAGE\fR, " \-\-in " \fIFOLDER\fR."
Output:
.BR \-\-sort " date|size|name, " \-\-limit " \fIN\fR, " \-\-paths ", " \-\-print0 ", " \-\-hidden .
Exits 1 when nothing matches.
.TP
.BR history " [\fIid\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR]"
List recent runs, or every move made by run \fIid\fR.
.TP
.BR undo " [\fIid\fR]"
Reverse the most recent run (or run \fIid\fR). Undoing an undo re-applies the run.
.TP
.BR config " [show|path|init|edit]"
Show the effective configuration, print the config file path, write a
commented starter file
.RB ( \-\-force
to overwrite), or open it in
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.BR completions " zsh|bash|fish"
Print a shell completion script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would happen without changing anything.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path " \fIDIR\fR"
Manage \fIDIR\fR instead of ~/Downloads.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Read configuration from \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print extra detail.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only errors and the final summary.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-journal
Do not record this run's moves (it cannot be undone).
.TP
.B \-\-time
Print how long the command took.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help; \fBfilemgr\fR \fIcommand\fR \fB\-\-help\fR for one command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH SIZES AND AGES
Sizes take an optional binary unit:
.BR K ", " M ", " G ", " T
(e.g. 1.5G). Ages take
.BR h ", " d ", " w ", " m " (30 days) or " y ;
a bare number means days.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is INI-style. Sections:
.TP
.B [general]
.BR root ", " remote ", " old_days ", " recent_count ", " threads .
.TP
.B [categories]
.IB FOLDER " = " "ext ext ..."
adds a category folder or replaces a built-in one's extensions.
.SH RULES
Each
.B [rule \(dqName\(dq]
section has an action and at least one condition:
.RS
.nf
[rule "Old installers"]
ext = dmg pkg
older = 14d
action = trash
.fi
.RE
.PP
Conditions:
.BR match " (globs), " ext ", " type ", " larger ", " smaller ", " older ", " newer ", "
.BR in " (top-level folder, or . for the top level). "
Actions:
.B trash
(move to ~/.Trash) or
.BI "move " FOLDER\fR.
.B enabled = false
disables a rule. Each file gets the first rule it matches.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FILEMGR_ROOT
Folder to manage (overridden by \fB\-\-path\fR).
.TP
.B FILEMGR_CONFIG
Config file path. Otherwise
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/filemgr/config " or " ~/.config/filemgr/config .
.TP
.B FILEMGR_STATE_DIR
Where the journal and watch lock live (default ~/.filemgr).
.TP
.B FILEMGR_TRASH
Where the \fBtrash\fR rule action moves files (default ~/.Trash).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/filemgr/config
Configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.filemgr/journal
Move journal used by \fBhistory\fR and \fBundo\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.filemgr/watch.lock
Held by a running \fBwatch\fR.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Logs/filemgr-watch.log
Log for the launchd agent generated by \fBwatch \-\-print\-plist\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a runtime error (or no matches for \fBfind\fR), 2 on a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
filemgr -n sort                 # preview sorting
filemgr dedup --near            # exact + near-duplicate images
filemgr find --larger 1G --sort size
filemgr stats --html report.html
filemgr clean --list
filemgr undo
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rclone (1),
.BR launchctl (1)
